---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import network from '../../data/expanded/network.json';
import products from '../../data/expanded/products.json';
const counts=Object.fromEntries(['hourly','daily','maintenance'].map(k=>[k,Object.values(network.reports).filter(r=>r[k].rows.length||r[k].entries.length).length]));
---
<BaseLayout title="Accessibility and review notes"><div class="plain-content"><h1>Accessibility and review notes</h1>
<p>The three sites preserve their original branding, navigation, colors, and desktop layouts, with changes for keyboard access, readable tables, small screens, and text alternatives.</p>
<h2>Available locally</h2><p>All 119 station pages; {counts.hourly} hourly reports, {counts.daily} daily reports and {counts.maintenance} maintenance logs; 100 recent raw station files; agricultural weather products and climate reference pages; and 27 current climate maps with local enlarged views.</p>
<p>Daily and hourly custom reports filter the available local dates and download CSVs. Eight reports for four retired stations are unavailable from the original source. Their pages say so explicitly.</p>
<h2>Updates</h2><p>Weather refreshes are scheduled hourly, subject to publisher and build availability. Climate maps update with matching dates, legends and regional text. Page timestamps identify saved source data; observation and forecast dates remain in the reports. This is not a streaming feed. Historical reference material is cached for up to 30 days.</p>
<h2>WCAG 2.2 AA target</h2><p>The site uses semantic headings, labelled controls, table headers, skip links, visible keyboard focus, keyboard-operated station selection, responsive layouts, and text for missing observations. The target follows <a href="https://webaccess.msu.edu/policy/technical-guidelines">MSU’s technical guidelines</a>.</p>
<p>This is an accessibility remediation preview for review, not an ADA certification or an institutional approval. Automated checks cannot establish full conformance. The newly expanded content has not received a new MSU Silktide score.</p>
<h2>Scope and remaining review</h2><ul><li>Historical database queries, five-minute data and the original growing-degree-day query engine require a supported source-data integration.</li><li>Recent three-hour raw files are mirrored; other raw archive folders are inventoried only.</li><li>Regional climate-map text contains approximate sampled color bands. It does not reproduce every underlying grid value.</li><li>Imported historical graphics, PDFs and fixed-width text reports need content-specific accessibility review. Source text and available companion data are retained.</li><li>Two agricultural temperature graphics are denied by the source server; related daily maximum and minimum station observations are available locally.</li><li>Separate NOAA, Wisconsin, partner and institutional services remain clearly external destinations.</li></ul>
<p>Production acceptance requires the site owners’ full-scope review, including manual assistive-technology checks, document/chart equivalents, and operational approval. <a href="https://webaccess.msu.edu/tools/silktide">MSU explains the limits of automated scans</a>.</p>
<p><a href="/enviroweather/review/">Meeting review report and coverage inventory</a></p><h2>Help</h2><p><a href="https://webaccess.msu.edu/">MSU Digital Accessibility</a> provides guidance and a <a href="https://go.msu.edu/digitalaccessibility">reporting service</a>.</p>
</div></BaseLayout>
